    body: "Rosalía has always been known for charting her own course as a pop star, and the Lux world tour is one of the clearest examples of that individuality. The Spanish artist takes the stage each night with dazzling visuals, ballet movements, and operatic vocals. Among the most original ideas woven into these elements is the \"confession\" segment, which expands on Lux's religious imagery.\n\nBuilt around a gothic confession booth reconstructed each evening, the segment invites a special guest onstage to make a confession to Rosalía; the singer then immediately launches into the sharp-tongued \"La Perla.\" The ritual both personalizes the stage show and ensures fans encounter a unique surprise each night.\n\nNumerous celebrities have appeared in the confession booth throughout the tour. Musicians, actors, and figures from the fashion world have shared small stories about breakups, jealousy, career regrets, and sometimes humorous misdeeds. These confessions have also gone viral on social media, elevating Lux beyond an ordinary arena show.\n\nFor Rosalía, Lux is both a musical and theatrical production; the confession booth stands out as her boldest attempt yet to place the relationship between religion, sin, and stardom at the heart of the show.",
